        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Bounded Rationality]]></title>
            <link>https://kerostig.org/call/elsevier-bounded-rationality-a-special-issue-in-honor-of-reinhard-selten/</link>
            <guid>elsevier-bounded-rationality-a-special-issue-in-honor-of-reinhard-selten</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:27:21 GMT</pubDate>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div>
    
    
    <p>This special issue honors the contributions of Reinhard Selten to the fields of bounded rationality, behavioral economics, and game theory. The issue invites submissions that advance our understanding of how cognitive limitations and bounded rationality shape economic behavior and decision-making.</p>
    
    <p>Contributions are welcome that explore the theoretical foundations and empirical applications of bounded rationality in various economic contexts, including but not limited to individual choice, strategic interaction, market behavior, and organizational decision-making.</p>
    
    
    <h2>Potential topics</h2>
    <ul>
        
        <li>Bounded rationality and economic behavior</li>
        
        <li>Decision-making under uncertainty</li>
        
        <li>Behavioral economics</li>
        
        <li>Cognitive limitations in economic decision-making</li>
        
        <li>Game theory and bounded rationality</li>
        
    </ul>
    
    
    <h2>Timeline</h2>
    <ul>
        
        <li>December 31, 2026: Full paper submission deadline</li>
        
    </ul>
    
    
</div>]]></content:encoded>
            <author>Journal of Economic Behavior &amp; Organization (ELSEVIER)</author>
        </item>
